<figure id="attachment_669" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-669" style="width: 800px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><a href="https://www.mapsofworld.com/answers/history/countries-won-world-war-ii/attachment/world-map-world-war-2-countries/" rel="attachment wp-att-669"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-669" src="https://images.mapsofworld.com/answers/2017/04/world-map-world-war-2-countries.jpg" alt="World Map showing Allied and Axis Countries" width="800" height="600" srcset="https://images.mapsofworld.com/answers/2017/04/world-map-world-war-2-countries.jpg 800w, https://images.mapsofworld.com/answers/2017/04/world-map-world-war-2-countries-150x113.jpg 150w, https://images.mapsofworld.com/answers/2017/04/world-map-world-war-2-countries-300x225.jpg 300w, https://images.mapsofworld.com/answers/2017/04/world-map-world-war-2-countries-768x576.jpg 768w, https://images.mapsofworld.com/answers/2017/04/world-map-world-war-2-countries-700x525.jpg 700w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" /></a><figcaption id="caption-attachment-669" class="wp-caption-text">World War II &#8211; Allied and Axis Countries</figcaption></figure>
<p>Two major alliances formed the basis of polarization during World War II. The war ended in a clear victory for the Allied Powers. The chief nations that made up the Allies are Great Britain, the Soviet Union, the United States, and China. France was also a significant Allied Nation but remained under Axis occupation between 1940 and 1944. The major Axis nations &#8211; <a href="/germany/">Germany</a>, <a href="/italy/">Italy</a>, and <a href="/japan/">Japan</a> were bound by strategic alliances such as the Anti-Comintern Pact and the Molotov–Ribbentrop Pact (Nazi-Soviet Pact). Several client states also supported the Axis powers.</p><div class='code-block code-block-5' style='margin: 8px 0; clear: both;'>
